   - Length variance (difference between outputs and references).
 - Report generation: structured JSON + Markdown summaries.
 - CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness.
+- Threshold validation with `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (can be repeated) for CI gating.
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Validation (CI Gating)
+- CLI supports `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) to fail evaluation if metrics fall below specified minimums.
+  - Example: `frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold length_variance=0.8`
+  - Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 if malformed.
+  - Valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`. Accepts custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`.
+  - Threshold minimum must be 0–1. A metric with no score (e.g., exact_match without references) fails its threshold.
+- Core `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9 }`) and adds `passed` (bool) and `thresholds` (list) to report.
+- Markdown and JSON reports document threshold results.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
